---
// /accessibility — the accessibility statement.
//
// Says only what was done. The check on 2026-09-26 ran axe-core 4.10.3 (WCAG
// 2.0, 2.1 and 2.2 A and AA rules, plus its best-practice rules) against every
// published page of this site at 1280px and 375px, and against ten pages of
// the documentation site. No manual screen-reader or keyboard-only audit has
// been done; the statement says so rather than implying one.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";

const reviewed = "2026-09-26";
const reviewedText = new Date(`${reviewed}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString("en-GB", {
  day: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  year: "numeric",
  timeZone: "UTC",
});
const mailto = `mailto:contact@odal-node.io?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Accessibility")}`;

const title = "Accessibility | Odal Node";
const description =
  "How accessible the Odal Node website is, how it was checked, what was fixed, what has not been tested yet, and how to tell us about a problem.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Section h1 eyebrow="Accessibility" title="This site should work for everyone who needs it.">
    <p>
      We aim for level AA of the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG)
      2.2 on this website and on the documentation site. This page says how
      far we have checked that, and where we have not yet.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600">
      Last reviewed <time datetime={reviewed}>{reviewedText}</time>.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="How it was checked" title="An automated check of every page." tone="muted">
    <p>
      We ran axe-core, a widely used automated checker, on every page of this
      site at desktop and phone widths, and on ten pages of the documentation
      site. It found three kinds of problem here, and all three are fixed:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Most pages had no main heading for a screen reader to start from.</li>
      <li>
        Some text was too faint to read comfortably: the station numbers on
        Lifecycle, past entries on the Timeline, and the withheld parts on
        Visibility, which now show as a dashed card instead of faded text.
      </li>
      <li>A box on the Verify page was marked as a separate page region when it was not one.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The documentation pages checked had no problems the checker could find.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Not yet tested" title="What an automated check cannot tell us.">
    <p>
      An automated checker finds only part of what makes a site hard to use.
      We have not yet tested this site from start to finish with a screen
      reader, or using only a keyboard, and we have not tested it with people
      who rely on either. Until we have, treat the parts that change as you use
      them, such as the menus, the passport check, the reader picker on
      Visibility and the file checker on Verify, as the most likely to have
      problems.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Tell us" title="Found something that does not work for you?" tone="tinted">
    <p>
      Email us with the page, what you were trying to do and what happened. We
      will reply, and fix it or say when we can.
    </p>
    <div class="not-prose mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <Button href={mailto}>Email contact@odal-node.io</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
